        }
      ],
      "explanation": "RC3 has a serious error. Although the doctor often advised not to self-adjust insulin and later repaired the plan, the earlier specific instruction to take 16 units based on an uncertain patient memory was an actionable, preventable medication-safety error in a diabetic patient.",
      "issue_kind": "commission",
      "rc_id": "RC3_diabetes_and_insulin_execution",
      "status": "serious_error"
    },
    {
